Subject: [PATCH] DIAGNOSTIC: arm crash handler before lock-acquire + pin acquire_instance_lock call (capture backtrace)
Target: prudynt-t @ f4b32289359d176fb0795d9f3735af0bd9d6d2fd (stacks on 0001-0014)

DIAGNOSTIC BUILD (throwaway). Prior diagnostic proved the startup SIGSEGV is in
acquire_instance_lock() -- proven Jun-26 code, unrelated to day/night -- which ran
BEFORE the crash handler was installed, so /tmp/prudynt_crash.log was never written.
0015's code never executes; its mere presence shifts the binary enough to fault.

This build:
  1. MOVES the sigaltstack + sigaction crash-handler install to the TOP of main(),
     BEFORE InstanceLockGuard/acquire (markers A1/A2), so the fault in acquire is
     now CAUGHT and dumped to /tmp/prudynt_crash.log with the register backtrace
     (EPC/RA + dladdr symbols) -- the exact libuclibcshim function + call chain.
  2. Adds unbuffered DIAG markers INSIDE acquire_instance_lock to pin the exact
     faulting call:
       acq1 = pre  std::filesystem::create_directories
       acq2 = post create_directories (so crash between acq1 and acq2 = filesystem)
       acq3 = post ::open
       acq4 = lock fully acquired
Keeps the daynight sidecar read (apply_daynight_sidecar) and the earlier A/D/E/F
markers. CFG::load()/Config.cpp byte-identical to proven.

Read it as: last DIAG line before "Segmentation fault" = the faulting statement;
"HANDLER entered" + a populated /tmp/prudynt_crash.log = the real backtrace.

Verified: git apply --check + patch -p1 both pass against f4b3228 + 0001-0014.

